a guard of honor at the holy see for  european parliament president martin  schulz making an official visit to pope  francis seven months after he began his  papacy it was a  extraordinary open-minded meeting we  spoke about lampedusa and the question  of a kind of immigration from regions  with civil wars  natural disasters  and hopelessness more than 300 illegal  immigrants mostly from north africa died  last week when their overcrowded vessel  caught fire and sank off lampadusa meps  held a minute silence for the victims  europe must prepare a strategy for  temporary protection and on the other  hand  we must discuss urgently  a system of legal  immigration into the european union  president schultz extended an invitation  to pope francis to address meps  something last seen exactly 25 years ago  in october 1988 when pope john paul ii  visited strasbourg  then it was on to the pontifical  gregorian university in rome for a  public discussion on the fight against  poverty and marginalization
 

